  <p>The x, y & z <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Vector#Components" target="_blank">components of the vector</a> are used to represent red, green, and blue respectively. The range is different from traditional RGB, instead of being 0 -> 255, LSL uses 0 -> 1. `<1.0, 1.0, 1.0>` represents "white" and `<0.0, 0.0, 0.0>` represents "black":</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`--  white & opaque
ll.SetText("I am white", vector(1.0, 1.0, 1.0), 1.0)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//  white & opaque
    llSetText("I am white", <1.0, 1.0, 1.0>, 1.0);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local myColor = ZERO_VECTOR  -- defaults to ZERO_VECTOR or <0.0, 0.0, 0.0> which is black
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector myColor;// defaults to ZERO_VECTOR or <0.0, 0.0, 0.0> which is black

    llSetText("I am black and 30% transparent.", myColor, 0.7);

    llSleep(7.5);   // before: <0.0, 0.0, 0.0> black
    myColor.x = 1.0;// now:    <1.0, 0.0, 0.0> red

    llSetText("I am now red and 10% transparent.", myColor, 0.9);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>If <b>alpha</b> is 1.0 it means the <b>text</b> is fully opaque (alpha), 0.0 would make it completely transparent (invisible):</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`ll.SetText("green text with alpha 0.7", vector(0.0, 1.0, 0.0), 0.7)

ll.SetText("white text with alpha 0.4\n60% transparent", vector(1.0, 1.0, 1.0), 0.4)
ll.SetText("white text with alpha 1.0\nfully opaque", vector(1.0, 1.0, 1.0), 1.0)

--  next to lines have the same effect
ll.SetText("invisible black text with alpha 0.0\nfully transparent", ZERO_VECTOR, 0)
ll.SetText("invisible black text with alpha 0.0\nfully transparent", vector(0.0, 0.0, 0.0), 0.0)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`llSetText("green text with alpha 0.7", <0.0, 1.0, 0.0>, 0.7);

    llSetText("white text with alpha 0.4\n60% transparent", <1.0, 1.0, 1.0>, 0.4);
    llSetText("white text with alpha 1.0\nfully opaque", <1.0, 1.0, 1.0>, 1.0);

//  next to lines have the same effect
    llSetText("invisible black text with alpha 0.0\nfully transparent", ZERO_VECTOR, 0);
    llSetText("invisible black text with alpha 0.0\nfully transparent", <0.0, 0.0, 0.0>, 0.0);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h3>Multiple lines</h3>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`--  two lines of orange text

ll.SetText("I am\non two lines!", vector(1.0, 0.4, 0.0), 1.0)`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`//  two lines of orange text

    llSetText("I am\non two lines!", <1.0, 0.4, 0.0>, 1.0);`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Useful Snippets</h2>
  <p>Drag this script out of inventory onto an object to erase its set text:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`-- http://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/llSetText

local function main()
    --      remove floating text (empty string & black & 100% transparent)
    ll.SetText("", ZERO_VECTOR, 0.0)

    --      delete the script as we only needed it to change the floating text property
    ll.RemoveInventory(ll.GetScriptName())
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`// http://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/llSetText

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
//      remove floating text (empty string & black & 100% transparent)
        llSetText("", ZERO_VECTOR, 0.0);

//      delete the script as we only needed it to change the floating text property
        llRemoveInventory(llGetScriptName());
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>Code to easily specify appearance of hovertext:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local NAVY = vector(0, 0.122, 0.247)
local BLUE = vector(0, 0.455, 0.851)
local AQUA = vector(0.498, 0.859, 1)
local TEAL = vector(0.224, 0.8, 0.8)
local OLIVE = vector(0.239, 0.6, 0.439)
local GREEN = vector(0.18, 0.8, 0.251)
local LIME = vector(0.004, 1, 0.439)
local YELLOW = vector(1, 0.863, 0)
local ORANGE = vector(1, 0.522, 0.106)
local RED = vector(1, 0.255, 0.212)
local MAROON = vector(0.522, 0.078, 0.294)
local FUCHSIA = vector(0.941, 0.071, 0.745)
local PURPLE = vector(0.694, 0.051, 0.788)
local WHITE = vector(1, 1, 1)
local SILVER = vector(0.867, 0.867, 0.867)
local GRAY = vector(0.667, 0.667, 0.667)
local BLACK = vector(0.000, 0.000, 0.000)

local hoverText = "TEXT GOES HERE"
local hoverColor = LIME  --  set predefined color or any RGB color vector in float form
local hoverAlpha = 1.0  -- Sets the text's transparency, 1.0 being opaque, while 0.0 would be transparent

local function main()
    ll.SetText(hoverText, hoverColor, hoverAlpha)
end

main()
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`vector NAVY    = <0,     0.122, 0.247>;
vector BLUE    = <0,     0.455, 0.851>;
vector AQUA    = <0.498, 0.859, 1    >;
vector TEAL    = <0.224, 0.8,   0.8  >;
vector OLIVE   = <0.239, 0.6,   0.439>;
vector GREEN   = <0.18,  0.8,   0.251>;
vector LIME    = <0.004, 1    , 0.439>;
vector YELLOW  = <1    , 0.863, 0    >;
vector ORANGE  = <1    , 0.522, 0.106>;
vector RED     = <1    , 0.255, 0.212>;
vector MAROON  = <0.522, 0.078, 0.294>;
vector FUCHSIA = <0.941, 0.071, 0.745>;
vector PURPLE  = <0.694, 0.051, 0.788>;
vector WHITE   = <1    , 1    , 1    >;
vector SILVER  = <0.867, 0.867, 0.867>;
vector GRAY    = <0.667, 0.667, 0.667>;
vector BLACK   = <0.000, 0.000, 0.000>;

string  hoverText   = "TEXT GOES HERE";
vector  hoverColor  = LIME;//  set predefined color or any RGB color vector in float form
float   hoverAlpha  = 1.0; // Sets the text's transparency, 1.0 being opaque, while 0.0 would be transparent

default
{
    state_entry()
    {
        llSetText(hoverText, hoverColor, hoverAlpha);
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <p>To make hovertext when using linked prims you can use this simple function:</p>
<div class="lua-block"><span class="tag lua-tag">Lua</span><DocsCode code={`local function mySetLinkText(linknum, text, color, alpha)
    ll.SetLinkPrimitiveParamsFast(linknum, {PRIM_TEXT, text, color, alpha})
end

-- For example:

function LLEvents.touch_start(events)
    local total_number = #events
    mySetLinkText(LINK_SET, "TEST", vector(0, 1, 0), 0.5)
end
`} lang="slua" /></div>
<div class="lsl-block"><span class="tag lsl-tag">LSL</span><DocsCode code={`mySetLinkText(integer linknum, string text, vector color, float alpha) {
    llSetLinkPrimitiveParamsFast(linknum, [PRIM_TEXT, text, color, alpha]);
}

// For example:

default
{
    touch_start(integer total_number)
    {
        mySetLinkText(LINK_SET, "TEST", <0, 1, 0>, 0.5);
    }
}`} lang="lsl" /></div>
  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <p>To actually display text on a prim, see <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/XyzzyText" target="_blank">XyzzyText</a>, or consider using parcel prim <a href="https://wiki.secondlife.com/wiki/Category:LSL_Media" target="_blank">Media</a> options (useful only if you have control over the land's media settings.)</p>
  <p>The function displays <b>text</b> that hover over the prim's center, the prim position. The height over the center is proportional to the prim's Z-dimension exclusively</p>
  <ul>
    <li>It doesn't matter how the prim is rotated, so if Z is smaller than X and Y the <b>text</b> may be seen <b>on</b> the prim</li>
  </ul>
